<div class="rn">
<h2>What&#x27;s New in 6.2</h2>
<h3 class="hl">Highlights</h3>
<ul class="highlights">
<li><strong>OpenCode sessions in the Quota Meter show their own burn rate.</strong> Each running OpenCode 2.x session shows its token rate, or its API-equivalent cost in the $ lens; free routes read Free. A row keeps its last rate for 5 minutes after a turn ends, marked idle, and has the same load bar as Codex and Claude. OpenCode has no quota or weekly figure yet.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Bug Fixes</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>An OpenCode request the provider refused no longer hides the session&#x27;s usage.</strong> One free-tier limit (HTTP 429) made Session Info show the whole session&#x27;s usage as unavailable. A refused request now counts as using no tokens.</li>
</ul>
<p class="more">Full release notes: <a href="https://github.com/jazzyalex/agent-sessions/releases/tag/v6.2">https://github.com/jazzyalex/agent-sessions/releases/tag/v6.2</a></p>
</div>
